#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0885 expect=violation domain=ADPPK
#note "FIX #154 NAME-TIER PIN -- this scenario was expect=skipped under D21 alone (-skipped-ADPPK-no-poppk-signature.cdt). The dataset is named ADPPK and is BDS (PARAMCD/AVAL) but carries no NONMEM column, so the column tier of AdamSubclassDetector yields nothing and there is no declaration either. Fix #154 adds a LAST-RESORT name tier -- AdamSubclassDetector.detectByName, consulted only after the columns AND the declaration are both silent -- which recognises ADPPK*/ADPPT*/ADPOPPK* on a BDS dataset as POPULATION PHARMACOKINETIC ANALYSIS. So the rule is selected and the absent USUBJIDN is reported. This deliberately reverses part of Fix #140, which removed the name tests assuming a declared tier is always available; D21-remainder rejected that assumption (1 of 33 define.xml files in /data/testdata carries any ADaM def:Class). The name is EVIDENCE inside a detector, not AUTHORITY in a rule's scope. Neuter by making AdamSubclassDetector.detectByName return null: no subclass is detected, the rule is skipped, and this scenario goes red. Its sibling CDISC-AD0885-skipped-ADPPT-undeclared-scope.cdt keeps the tier honest -- ADPPT with no BDS indicator is still SKIPPED, because the name tier requires BASIC DATA STRUCTURE."
# Rule:Description: Raise an error when USUBJIDN is not present in an ADPPKIG v1.0 dataset.
#expectViolationCount 1
dataset ADPPK
col STUDYID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col AVAL    type=Num
---
CDISCPILOT01 | CONC | 12.5
---
